{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Start with the Maclaurin series for $e^x$.\n\n$\\displaystyle e^x=1\\text{ }+\\text{ }x\\text{ }+\\text{ }\\frac{{{x}^{2}}}{2!}\\text{ }+\\text{ }\\frac{{{x}^{3}}}{3!}\\text{ }+\\ldots +\\text{ }\\frac{{{x}^{n}}}{n!}\\text{ }+\\ldots \\,$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Substitute $3x$ for $x$.\n\n$\\displaystyle e^{3x}=1\\text{ }+3x\\text{ }+\\text{ }\\frac{9{{x}^{2}}}{2!}\\text{ }+\\text{ }\\frac{27{{x}^{3}}}{3!}\\text{ }+\\ldots +\\text{ }\\frac{{{(3x)}^{n}}}{n!}\\text{ }+\\ldots$\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Multiply by $\\dfrac{2}{3}$.\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\frac{2}{3}e^{3x}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{2}{3}+2x+\\dfrac{6{{x}^{2}}}{2!}+\\dfrac{18{{x}^{3}}}{3!}+\\ldots +\\dfrac{2{{(3x)}^{n}}}{3n!}\\text{ }+\\ldots\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{2}{3}+2x+3x^2+3x^3+\\ldots+\\dfrac{2{{(3x)}^{n}}}{3n!}+\\ldots\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"The first three non-zero terms are\n\n$\\dfrac{2}{3}+2x+3x^2$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**What are the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin polynomial for the function $f(x)=\\dfrac{2}{3}{{e}^{3x}}$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\frac{2}{3}+2x+3x^2$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\displaystyle2+2x+3x^2$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle 1+3x+\\frac{9x^2}{2!}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\frac{2}{3}+3x+6x^2$","correct":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
